Scope note, because this repository sits next to other people's licences:

  * Everything written here - tools/, initramfs/init, src/, rootfs/overlay/,
    docs/, tests/ - is the MIT-licensed work above.
  * The kernel tree this project builds
    (github.com/amazon-oss/android_kernel_amazon_mtk8163, branch
    cronos/lineage-18.1) is GPL-2.0 and is cloned at build time, never vendored.
    Building or distributing a kernel image from it puts you under GPL-2.0 for
    that image.
  * Alpine packages installed into the rootfs keep their own licences, which the
    package database in the image records.
  * The Amazon bootloader, TEE and preloader are proprietary and are not
    redistributed here in any form.
